<%#
  Birthday modal — the entry-time DOB gate (ENABLE_AGE_GATE). Mounted by the
  modal host as id 'birthday'; opened from the onboarding chain (step 2) and
  from the contest hold-to-confirm flow before the Get Entry Tokens modal.

  THE CARD IS THE ENGINE'S (studio/modals/blocks/_birthday, adopted 2026-08-26).
  This app rendered its own copy — modals/_age_verify — until the engine homed it
  at 0.60.1. All that is left here is the chain's position pill and the locals
  BirthdayModalHelper resolves, because the engine hardcodes no legal policy.

  THE REFUSAL IS NO LONGER THIS CARD'S JOB. The deleted fork turned red and
  disabled its own submit button on an under-age date — the one screen state with
  nothing to press and nowhere to go. Now the date submits like any other and the
  SERVER's verdict routes: /age/verify answers `underage: true`, and the engine
  factory swaps to the 'age-gate' card, which carries the two ways out (watch
  instead, or fix the date).

  PILL PLACEMENT. The pill sits ABOVE the engine card rather than inside it. The
  engine block has no yield slot, and this is where the chain's other two steps
  already put theirs (modals/_onboarding at 1 of 3, modals/_wallet_setup at 3 of
  3, both at card top level) — so step 2 now matches its siblings instead of
  being the one that tucked the pill under the title.

  Single root element (template-x-if mount rule).
%>
<div>
  <%# Step 2 of the onboarding chain — see the note in modals/_onboarding.
      SHOWN UNCONDITIONALLY, including when the entry gate opens this card on its
      own for a user who never walked the chain. That is the operator's call and
      the simpler rule; if a standalone DOB prompt claiming "2 of 3" ever reads
      wrong, gate it on a prop the chain driver passes rather than guessing from
      session state. %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/progress_pill", current: 2, total: 3 %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/birthday", **birthday_modal_locals %>
</div>
